 "title": "Hail, Poetry",
 "description": "The unaccompanied chorus from Act I of The Pirates of Penzance, as Sullivan printed it: the pirates, the Major-General and his daughters hail poetry together in full, loud chords. Short, stately and all homophonic, with a few chromatic turns in the tenor and alto. The 1st and 2nd sopranos are the soprano and alto here; the tenor and the 2nd bass line are the tenor and bass (the 1st basses' middle notes are left out).",
 "difficulty": "intermediate",
